-- title:
--   Framing of a locally principal ideal sheaf by a nonzerodivisor generator
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme, let $I$ be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf datum on $X$ (an `IdealSheafData`), let $W$ be an open subset of $X$ and let $a \in \Gamma(X,W)$ be a section of the structure sheaf. Write `I.module` for the sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_X$-modules obtained as the kernel of the canonical map from the unit module $\mathcal{O}_X$ to the pushforward along the closed immersion `I.subschemeι` of the unit module of the associated closed subscheme, and write `I.moduleι` for the canonical morphism from `I.module` to the unit module, so that on an affine open $U$ its component is an injection onto the ideal $I(U) \subseteq \Gamma(X,U)$. Assume that for every affine open $U$ of $X$ contained in $W$ the ideal $I(U)$ is the principal ideal generated by the restriction $a|_U$, and that $a|_U$ is a nonzerodivisor in $\Gamma(X,U)$. Then there exists a section $e \in \Gamma(I.\mathrm{module}, W)$ such that `I.moduleι` sends $e$ to $a$ and such that $e$ is a frame on $W$, that is: for every open $W' \subseteq W$ the map $\Gamma(X,W') \to \Gamma(I.\mathrm{module},W')$, $g \mapsto g \cdot (e|_{W'})$, is bijective.
--
--   The statement says that on an open where a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf is generated, affine-locally, by the restrictions of a single nonzerodivisor section $a$, the corresponding sheaf of modules $\mathcal{O}_X(-Z)$ is free of rank one on that open, with a distinguished generator lifting $a$. It feeds the construction of frames for tensor products of such invertible ideal modules, used in [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_isFrameOn_invModule_tensor_module_of_ideal_eq_span`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_isFrameOn_invModule_tensor_module_of_ideal_eq_span).
